### StudentApi HTTP Testing
### Uncomment and run these requests to test the API
### Requires: Visual Studio or REST Client extension in VS Code

@baseUrl = https://localhost:7001
@accessToken = 

### 1. LOGIN - Get JWT Token (Admin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "Admin@123"
}

### 2. LOGIN - Get JWT Token (Regular User)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "user",
  "password": "User@123"
}

### 3. GET All Students (Requires Auth)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/student
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 4. GET Student by ID (Requires Auth)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/student/1
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 5. CREATE Student (Requires Admin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/student
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "age": 21,
  "course": "Computer Science"
}

###

### 6. CREATE Student (Invalid - will return 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/student
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "J",
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "age": 15,
  "course": ""
}

###

### 7. UPDATE Student (Requires Admin)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/student/1
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Doe",
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "age": 22,
  "course": "Data Science"
}

###

### 8. DELETE Student (Requires Admin)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/student/1
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 9. Test 401 Unauthorized (No Token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/student
Accept: application/json

###

### 10. Test 403 Forbidden (Non-Admin creating student)
### First login as 'user' (non-admin) and get token
### Then try to POST a student - should return 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/student
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alice Smith",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "age": 20,
  "course": "Information Technology"
}

###

### 11. Swagger UI
GET {{baseUrl}}/

###
